+# UC-29 Create collection design
+
+Binding design: UC28 PR89 merged, fresh isolated develop tree equals the tested 6559-pass tree; nine current documents reloaded and hashes matched; automatic Gate1 passed under the authorized batch.
+
+## Intent and scope
+
+Implement issue30, UC29 main flow and AF01..05, FR-CL01 and initial BR05/06 relationships. An active authenticated owner creates a private owned collection from opaque native ciphertext, with permitted initial profile, folder and record identifiers. Ownership comes only from current identity. The server never decrypts content or creates usable keys. Existing collection/member schema and complete native protection inventory are already present; no migration, dependency, grant, collection read/update/delete or membership replacement endpoint is added. Later UCs30..37 own those flows.
+
+Dedicated strict command and dedicated guarded PostgreSQL store follow current folder/record creation conventions. Reusing the profile association resolver would require a broader interface and includes foreign collection attachment semantics unsuitable for owned member creation. Deferring initial members to UC34 would leave the UC29 submitted relationships incomplete. The dedicated flow is the chosen approach.
+
+## Public contract
+
+POST `/api/collections`, current Heimdall bearer identity, exactly one canonical `X-Cerberus-Vault-Access` handle, no query, bounded strict UTF8 JSON/no BOM/compression/duplicate/unknown/case-forged fields. All responses no-store. Shared oversized response is actually empty413.
+
+Exactly six required input fields: `collectionId`, `envelope`, `editedAt`, `profileIds`, `recordIds`, `folderIds`. Use a client-chosen canonical lowercase dashed nonzero UUID before encryption. Envelope is current `cerberus-content-v1` with initial KeyEpoch1 and native canonical binary fields. UTC editedAt must be at least year0001 first microsecond and is floored to UTC microseconds before PostgreSQL binding, including pre2000 times. Each ID array is nonnull, unique within its kind and contains only nonzero canonical UUIDs. Empty arrays are meaningful; same UUID across different typed arrays is permitted. No plaintext name/fields, owner, epoch override, grants, proof/challenge, expected parent revisions, access/session overrides or encryption wrappers are accepted.
+
+201 `collection_created`: exactly collectionId/revision/serverSequence/editedAt; revision1, positive safe integer sequence<=9007199254740991, stored normalized UTC time. No internal IDs, ownership, linked content, keys or credentials in success. Name is required in the encrypted client payload and cannot be inspected server-side.
+
+`CollectionCreateInput(Guid CollectionId,EncryptedEnvelope Envelope,DateTimeOffset EditedAt,Guid[] ProfileIds,Guid[] RecordIds,Guid[] FolderIds)` with strict JSON attributes/IsValid; `CollectionCreateRequest(Guid Actor,string AccessVerifier,CollectionCreateInput Input)`; `CollectionCreateDetails(Guid CollectionId,long Revision,long ServerSequence,DateTimeOffset EditedAt)`; `ICollectionCreateStore.CreateAsync(request,ct):Task<VaultResult<CollectionCreateDetails>>`. Application CreateCollectionCommand/Handler/Validator/Output/Messages mirror sibling contracts, trusted actor/hashed access only. Store `CollectionCreateStore(IDbContextFactory<AppDbContext>)`. New CollectionsController POST action and exactly three explicit registrations.
+
+## Authority and permitted relationships
+
+Current actor must map to an active nonterminal account and a current unrevoked own session, matching current positive policy/generation, IssuedAt<=database statement time, exclusive valid expiry when renewal enabled or explicit null expiry when disabled. A selection must remain an owned active nonterminal profile; never clear ProfileId to broaden access.
+
+Account-wide permits empty links or multiple owned active profile links. Selected access requires exactly its current profile in profileIds; empty is403, other/multiple/foreign profile targets404. All requested folders and records must be owned by the actor's account, active/nonterminal and have complete active same-owner folder ancestry. Account-wide admits these owned members. Selection admits folders only through its PF ancestor routes or selected owned PC/CF routes; records additionally through direct PR or selected owned PC/CR routes. A record-only route never admits its containing folder. Direct child/member permission never reveals private ancestors or siblings. Relevant visible active cycles503; hidden/incomplete ancestors404 before corrupt opaque/native state probing. Unrelated cycles do not affect this create.
+
+Foreign native RO/RW content cannot become a member of an actor-owned collection, even after actual successful native GET; return404 without changing either graph. No new grant or recipient access is created. Existing grants/keys/pins/protection and foreign/recipient metadata remain unchanged. Owned grouping does not decrypt or repair existing member ciphertext and does not require an unrelated native-grant proof. Unchanged owned authorization collections contribute only active typed membership routes: their unused opaque cipher or revision/sequence counters are not parsed or repaired, matching the existing creation boundary; there is no AF06/key-provisioning transition here. Selected initial membership cannot select an owned private root through the new collection: every member already needs current selected visibility before insertion.
+
+## Atomic storage and ordering
+
+Own account UPDATE and matching session UPDATE first. Requested/selected owned profiles in publicUUID order NO KEY UPDATE, then active owned effective collections contributing to requested member paths in publicUUID order NO KEY UPDATE, then distinct requested folders UPDATE and requested records UPDATE in publicUUID order. No foreign account/profile/grant locks and no upward ancestry UPDATE chain. This shares collection-before-content order with native recipient editors. Strong ownaccount serializes supported owner creation/move/trash/profile-association/protection writers and their account FKs. No recipient-account grant FK is added; BEFOREUC35 audit remains mandatory.
+
+Capture at most requested members, their complete ancestry, typed PF/PR/CF/CR/PC routes, requested/selected profile state and effective owned collections. Re-evaluate current authority after every potentially waiting phase. A lost current permission/account/session/member/profile/ancestry lifecycle has its current404/403 outcome before duplicate or stale/corrupt metadata probes. Compare the captured stable snapshot/held scope again in the guarded INSERT with statement-time session and lifecycle predicates. Changed valid inventory or an unheld earlier resource returns409/reload instead of adding locks after content. Conservative valid member edits can require retry even without caller expected member revisions; no winning ciphertext may be overwritten.
+
+The guarded new collection INSERT is the authorization linearization point. Once permitted under held locks, completing the atomic operation is allowed after later natural expiry. Insert original envelope bytes, immutable account, KeyEpoch1, revision1, normalized client time and safe new global sequence; verify stored metadata/bytes before success. Existing retained or typed terminal collectionID409; different-kind sameUUID markers do not block a collection. Duplicate races have one winner and lost-success replay409 preserves it.
+
+Create all requested PC/CF/CR links in separate counted SQL batches inside the same transaction, so each actual mutation stage has a fault boundary. Each distinct directly linked owned profile, folder and record advances structural revision/serverSequence/stamp exactly once; preserve their opaque content, client times, parent/protection/trash/other relationships. Overlapping folder+contained direct record routes remain distinct typed links, with one bump per explicitly submitted entity. Ancestors, inherited descendants, nonlinked profiles and recipients do not get fabricated bumps. Current GET/list recalculates inheritance; UC48 must supply durable inherited visibility before release.
+
+Validate changed parent/member counters positive safe and below maximum revision, normalized nondefault UTC microsecond EditedAt and consistent active nullPurgeAt. Visible required structural corruption503; exhausted revision/global sequence409. Sequence must exceed each changed row's previous sequence; regressed allocation503 and whole rollback. Sequence gaps after rollback are allowed. INSERT, any link stage, any profile/folder/record bump and post-write verification faults roll back the whole graph; a clean sameID retry after failed transaction can succeed. Catch supported persistence/timeout/provider and wrapped failures/internal cancellation as safe503; propagate caller cancellation. Never return success on malformed stored details or error-with-data.
+
+## Flow mapping and verification
+
+Main: strict input→trusted current owner scope→resolve every permitted owned relationship→atomic INSERT/PC+CF+CR/structural counters→201 exact4.
+AF01: strict input/envelope/time/typed array/canonical UUID/transport400, empty413; assert no graph mutation. AF02: current hidden/foreign/trashed/terminal/out-of-selection relationship/account or hidden ancestry404, native foreign GET thencreate404. AF03: missing/current-invalid identity401; missing access401; revoked/expired/policy/generation/selection or selectedempty403 with no mutation. AF04: duplicate retained/reserved ID, concurrent/replayed winning create, changed captured state/unheld resource, exhausted safe counters409; preserve winner. AF05: required dependency/visible structural/ancestry corruption503, no partial associations or metadata; caller cancellation propagates internally.
+
+Command tests use actual source-linked canonical converter and literal independent success keys; every required field/array and distinct timestamp boundary. Data realPostgreSQL tests cover wide/selected PF/PR/ownedPC CF/CR/nested folders/multiple profiles/collections/cross-kind sameUUID/foreign native denials, exact immutable fullgraphs and metadata. Natural expiry at account/session/profile/collection/folder/record waits and finalINSERT; current terminal/policy/scope removal during waits; changed existing memberships/ancestry/beforeINSERT unheld routes409. Controlled current owner create/move/trash/association/rotation and native recipient edit races bothorders preserve winners/no deadlocks. Actual post-INSERT/link/profile/folder/record faultTriggered asserts full rollback and sameID cleanretry; sequence exhausted/regressed boundaries. EXPLAIN requested candidates/path shape among unrelated inventories and exact held IDs/no upward/foreign locks.
+
+Actual native HTTP creates new collections, real profiles/folders/records and selectedMaster/PerProfile sessions; subsequent existing profile/folder/record GET/list confirms actual initial relationships/inheritance and hidden-reference filtering. Shared strict-body fixture MUST have a real valid-body control before invalid mutations. Current rotation already includes all collections: after real create, native complete inventory including new collection and legitimate typed aliases succeeds, omitted/extra/stale/foreign replacements fail before proof consumption; rewrap preserves collection and links. Ordinary native corpus322×4/audits153/helpers/lockedrestore/spec/OpenAPI/fullfresh6families>=90lineeach/aggregatebranch/ONEwholebranchreview/exacthead3CI required. Independent formal crypto/security/protocol/client qualification remains development-only deferred, release/main/tag gates intact.
+
+## Five review priorities
+
+- Selected creation must not attach an owned private member or foreign native recipient item, including record-only routes and mixed direct/inherited collection paths.
+- Authority must remain current through every wait and the INSERT, with natural expiry or typed terminal/scope changes denying before uniqueness or stale metadata leaks.
+- Collection-before-content order must serialize current owner and native recipient writers without foreign-account or upward-chain deadlocks; changed captured or unheld routes require reload.
+- Collection, every initial typed link and every distinct directly affected structural counter must commit together or fully roll back after actual mutations; opaque bytes, times, prior trash and winner state remain exact.
+- A newly created collection must enter complete native rotation inventory without widening selected sessions, inventing usable keys or claiming durable inherited visibility/client qualification.
